# ZebraSGDCommands - Utility Methods Only

_Last updated: 2025-08-06_

## 🚨 CRITICAL: This Class is for UTILITIES ONLY

The [ZebraSGDCommands](mdc:lib/zebra_sgd_commands.dart) class has been **refactored** to contain ONLY utility methods for data detection and parsing. **ALL command generation methods have been removed** and moved to the command pattern architecture.

**See also:**
- [Command Usage Guide](mdc:.cursor/rules/command-usage-guide.mdc) - Section 8 for usage patterns
- [Command Implementation Guide](mdc:.cursor/rules/command-implementation-guide.mdc) - For creating new commands
- [CommandFactory](mdc:lib/internal/commands/command_factory.dart) - For all command generation

## Purpose

[ZebraSGDCommands](mdc:lib/zebra_sgd_commands.dart) provides utility methods for:
- ✅ **Data format detection** - Identifying ZPL vs CPCL data
- ✅ **Response parsing** - Extracting values from SGD responses
- ✅ **Format detection** - Determining printer language from data
- ❌ **NOT for command strings** - Use CommandFactory instead

## Current Implementation

The class now contains ONLY these methods:

```dart
class ZebraSGDCommands {
  /// Check if data is ZPL format
  static bool isZPLData(String data);
  
  /// Check if data is CPCL format
  static bool isCPCLData(String data);
  
  /// Determine printer language from data
  static PrintFormat? detectDataLanguage(String data);
  
  /// Parse SGD response to extract value
  static String? parseResponse(String response);
}
```

**Note:** The `isLanguageMatch` method mentioned in some documentation has also been removed. Use direct comparison or the format detection methods instead.

## Methods That NO LONGER EXIST

The following methods have been **REMOVED** and will cause **runtime errors** if called:

### Command Generation (REMOVED)
- ❌ `getCommand(String setting)` → Use `CommandFactory.createGetSettingCommand()`
- ❌ `setCommand(String setting, String value)` → Use appropriate CommandFactory method
- ❌ `doCommand(String action, String value)` → Use appropriate CommandFactory method

### Mode Commands (REMOVED)
- ❌ `setZPLMode()` → Use `CommandFactory.createSendSetZplModeCommand()`
- ❌ `setCPCLMode()` → Use `CommandFactory.createSendSetCpclModeCommand()`

### Control Commands (REMOVED)
- ❌ `resetPrinter()` → Use appropriate CommandFactory method
- ❌ `unpausePrinter()` → Use `CommandFactory.createSendUnpauseCommand()`
- ❌ `resumePrinter()` → Use `CommandFactory.createSendUnpauseCommand()`
- ❌ `clearAlerts()` → Use `CommandFactory.createSendClearAlertsCommand()`

### ZPL Commands (REMOVED)
- ❌ `zplResume()` → Use `CommandFactory.createSendUnpauseCommand()`
- ❌ `zplClearErrors()` → Use `CommandFactory.createSendZplClearErrorsCommand()`
- ❌ `zplClearBuffer()` → Use `CommandFactory.createSendZplClearBufferCommand()`
- ❌ `zplFlushBuffer()` → Use `CommandFactory.createSendZplFlushBufferCommand()`

### CPCL Commands (REMOVED)
- ❌ `cpclClearBuffer()` → Use `CommandFactory.createSendCpclClearBufferCommand()`
- ❌ `cpclFlushBuffer()` → Use `CommandFactory.createSendCpclFlushBufferCommand()`
- ❌ `cpclClearErrors()` → Use `CommandFactory.createSendCpclClearErrorsCommand()`

## Usage Examples

### ✅ CORRECT - Using Utility Methods
```dart
import 'package:zebrautil/zebra_sgd_commands.dart';

// Data format detection
if (ZebraSGDCommands.isZPLData(printData)) {
  // Handle ZPL data
  await CommandFactory.createSendZplClearBufferCommand(printer).execute();
} else if (ZebraSGDCommands.isCPCLData(printData)) {
  // Handle CPCL data
  await CommandFactory.createSendCpclClearBufferCommand(printer).execute();
}

// Format detection
final format = ZebraSGDCommands.detectDataLanguage(printData);
if (format == PrintFormat.zpl) {
  // Use ZPL-specific commands
}

// Response parsing
final sgdResponse = '"device.languages" : "zpl"';
final value = ZebraSGDCommands.parseResponse(sgdResponse); // Returns: "zpl"
```

### ❌ WRONG - These Will Cause Runtime Errors
```dart
// ❌ ALL OF THESE WILL FAIL AT RUNTIME
final command = ZebraSGDCommands.zplClearErrors(); // NoSuchMethodError
_printer!.sendCommand(ZebraSGDCommands.unpausePrinter()); // NoSuchMethodError
final sgd = ZebraSGDCommands.getCommand('device.languages'); // NoSuchMethodError
ZebraSGDCommands.setZPLMode(); // NoSuchMethodError
ZebraSGDCommands.clearAlerts(); // NoSuchMethodError
```

### ✅ CORRECT - Use CommandFactory Instead
```dart
import 'package:zebrautil/internal/commands/command_factory.dart';

// Clear errors based on format
if (format == PrintFormat.zpl) {
  await CommandFactory.createSendZplClearErrorsCommand(printer).execute();
} else {
  await CommandFactory.createSendCpclClearErrorsCommand(printer).execute();
}

// Unpause printer
await CommandFactory.createSendUnpauseCommand(printer).execute();

// Get printer setting
final command = CommandFactory.createGetSettingCommand(printer, 'device.languages');
final result = await command.execute();

// Set printer mode
await CommandFactory.createSendSetZplModeCommand(printer).execute();

// Clear alerts
await CommandFactory.createSendClearAlertsCommand(printer).execute();
```

## Migration Guide

If you have code that uses the old ZebraSGDCommands methods:

1. **Remove** any calls to command generation methods
2. **Replace** with appropriate CommandFactory methods
3. **Keep** only the utility method calls for data detection and parsing

### Before (OLD - Will Fail)
```dart
// Command generation
final cmd = ZebraSGDCommands.zplClearErrors();
await printer.sendCommand(cmd);

// Mode setting
await printer.sendCommand(ZebraSGDCommands.setZPLMode());

// SGD commands
final setting = ZebraSGDCommands.getCommand('device.languages');
await printer.sendCommand(setting);
```

### After (NEW - Correct)
```dart
// Command generation
await CommandFactory.createSendZplClearErrorsCommand(printer).execute();

// Mode setting
await CommandFactory.createSendSetZplModeCommand(printer).execute();

// SGD commands
await CommandFactory.createGetSettingCommand(printer, 'device.languages').execute();
```

## Integration with Parser Utilities

For more advanced parsing needs, consider using [ParserUtil](mdc:lib/internal/parser_util.dart) in conjunction with ZebraSGDCommands:

```dart
// Parse SGD response and convert to appropriate type
final response = await printer.getSetting('device.pause');
final value = ZebraSGDCommands.parseResponse(response); // "true" or "false"
final isPaused = ParserUtil.toBool(value) ?? false; // Convert to bool
```

## Summary

- ✅ **DO** use ZebraSGDCommands for data format detection
- ✅ **DO** use ZebraSGDCommands for parsing SGD responses
- ❌ **DON'T** call any command generation methods (they don't exist)
- ❌ **DON'T** expect methods that were removed to work
- ✅ **DO** use CommandFactory for all command generation needs

